.DS_Store

# Runtime-generated — both created automatically by the app at startup
# (see server/db/client.js and server/index.js). Contains local player
# data / uploaded match-recommendation files — never commit these.
#
# `server/data` is written as a CONTENTS GLOB rather than a directory, because
# the seeds below have to be re-included and git will not un-ignore a file
# whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded. That is measured, not assumed: adding the
# bare spelling `server/data` here makes `!server/data/seeds/*.json` stop
# matching, because git never descends into an excluded directory.
#
# `server/uploads` therefore carries the dual spelling alone. The trailing
# slash matches a DIRECTORY only; a SYMLINK of the same name is not matched by
# it, which is how `server/data` and `server/uploads` were once committed as
# absolute symlinks into a developer's home directory — dangling on any other
# machine, and client.js's mkdirSync then throws ENOENT at import before the
# database is opened. `server/data` cannot take that guard without losing the
# seeds; the contents glob still ignores everything a symlink would have
# shadowed, and client.js's own startup guard covers the rest.
server/data/*
# ...except the verified-domain seeds, which are not data. Each row is the
# written evidence for one athletics host — the official institution page that
# links to it and what the host says it is — and the tests read it to hold the
# two-anchor rule. A ledger row is only as good as the account beside it, and
# that account belongs in history.
!server/data/seeds/
server/data/seeds/*
!server/data/seeds/*.json
server/uploads/
server/uploads

# Generated public profile pages
build/

# esbuild output for the Pages worker
worker/dist/

# Generated client report artefacts — never commit these
server/reports/
